applied, proposed 2 times: lambdas that only forward their argument to one method (b->b.x(), x->foo(x), (a,b)->meet(a,b)) become method references (B::x, this::foo, this::meet); refused where the reference needs a fully qualified name (s->s.parameters() -> fearlessFullGrammar.Sig::parameters)
applied, proposed 1 time: an Optional tested by hand then unwrapped with get() (o.isPresent()&&o.get().equals(x), o.isEmpty()?d:f(o.get()), a.isEmpty()?b:a) becomes one Optional expression (o.equals(Optional.of(x)), o.map(f).orElse(d), a.or(..), flatMap); early-return guards stay
applied, proposed 3 times: 'same -> return old' shortcuts on data holding no E (IT, List<IT>, Sig, MSigL, bound lists, TypeRename IT overloads) in inference/inject are deleted and the new value is always built, as the InjectionSteps header asks; refused for core T (T.RCC.withTs/withRC, TypeRename of(T)/ofT: type checker path, outside the header's scope), for fixArity(List<M>) (M identity) and for dropMethBs's methBs.isEmpty (it changes the result)
applied, proposed 3 times: a static helper B.xs(List<B>) replacing the repeated bs.stream().map(B::x).toList() chain (refused twice as a new concept; applied on the third proposal, which showed single use locals inlined and methods losing lines)
applied, proposed 1 time: two parallel lists walked by index with a hand written size assert (for i: Range.of(xs) f(xs.get(i),ys.get(i)), IntStream.range(..).mapToObj(i->..)) become Streams.zip(xs,ys), which pairs and asserts equal length; loops using i itself stay
applied, proposed 1 time: a null or index assert right before code that already fails on the same bad value (assert d!=null; d.ms(), assert i!=-1; ts[i]) is deleted; when the value is only returned it becomes Objects.requireNonNull
applied, proposed 1 time: a condition read out of an Optional with a literal default (o.map(p).orElse(false), o.map(p).orElse(true), o.filter(p).isPresent()) becomes o.stream().anyMatch(p) / o.stream().allMatch(p)
applied, proposed 1 time: a list of n copies of one value built by a generated stream (Stream.generate(()->v).limit(n), IntStream.range(0,n).mapToObj(_->v)) becomes Collections.nCopies(n,v), except where the list reaches Require.unmodifiable (it does not accept Collections$CopiesList)
applied, proposed 1 time: switch arms over type forms where RCX/ReadImmX repeat the X arm on the wrapped X (case RCX(_,var x) -> <same body as X>) recurse on x instead (case RCX(_,var x) -> f(x,..)), leaving the X arm as the only copy
applied, proposed 1 time: a filtered stream collected into a List only to test isEmpty()/size()==1 and take getFirst() becomes OneOr.of/OneOr.opt, or noneMatch when only emptiness matters
applied, proposed 1 time: an isEmpty() branch in front of Join.of(xs,open,sep,close,empty) is deleted, its result moving into the empty argument or into open/close, since Join.of already handles the empty list
applied, proposed 1 time: hand built concatenations with nested Stream.concat or list->stream->concat->list become Commons Streams.of(a,b,c) or Push.of(list,list|elem)
applied, proposed 1 time: if/else whose branches make the same call or assignment with different values becomes one call or assignment with a ?: argument (l= c ? a : b; e.line(c ? s1 : s2)); not when the condition would have to be repeated
applied, proposed 1 time: helpers taking a value plus parts derivable from it (x, x.span().inner; rcc.rc(), rcc.span(), rcc.c().name(), rcc.c().ts(); a record field already in scope) take the one value and derive the rest
applied, proposed 1 time: a map get followed by a null test and a fallback (v= m.get(k); v!=null?v:d) becomes m.getOrDefault(k,d)
